# gae-accounts-signal — V2 execution

When the user asks for an account-signals run, digest, or SOP execution in this folder:

1. Follow `sops/sop-master-digest-v2.md` and the three stage SOPs it names. Do not follow `v1-archived/`.
2. Load every populated row from `account-context/GAE_Top_Accounts_Context_23september.xlsx` (or the derived snapshot only if it still matches that workbook). Reason on filled Q2 values as breadth of AIHR reach within HR. See `account-context/README.md`.
3. Use one continuous review window. Do not lengthen it to fill a quiet digest. Do not backfill months of missed weeks unless the user asks.
4. Write all outputs under `runs/{run-id}/`. Include the queries actually run, candidates, early enrichment suppresses, final Include/Suppress decisions, and the account-context fields used for each included or suppressed candidate.
5. Hiring volume, a bare leadership appointment, an HR-system go-live, awards, and generic leadership commentary are not standalone signals.
6. Separate fact from hypothesis in anything an Account Manager could see.
7. Rep-level Slack routing is off. One combined test digest may go to Slack DM `D01DFNA0GBH`. Do not invent other destinations. Suppressed and silent accounts stay out of that digest.
8. If research cannot be finished, stop with a checkpoint that names the unfinished accounts. Do not mark those accounts silent.
